Restore the GL context before asynchronous query polling.

Source: virglrenderer 1.3.0, ca50e008863837e094747a69974dde3ae148aeaa
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/virglrenderer/+/refs/tags/1.3.0/

The caller (for example QEMU's display backend) can change the current GL
context between polling calls. The synchronous fence path resets the cached
context before checking queries; the asynchronous path needs the same reset.
Without it, query reads can run in the wrong GL context and return undefined
results. Tested with QEMU 11.1.1, the native gpu(3) query reproducer and
vmx/test/virgl.c inside Void Linux; see boot/VOID.md.

